  "term": "IPSP",
  "definition": "IPSP stands for inhibitory postsynaptic potential, a local change at a target neuron's synaptic membrane during neurotransmission that makes the membrane more negatively charged. This reduces the neuron's responsiveness to excitatory signals.",
